nnot assume those runtimes share one physical browser record. Bound its ownership and cross-tab coordination explicitly. Preserve deviceB's discovery of recorded work and exact settlement without silently adding journal sync or a broader authority model. R4/C4/C5 should cover the precise guarantee at the cheap actual persistence/transport boundary.\n\n3. Count platform sends as well as the G15 loop. Section13 says the publication handler emits at most32 link messages and therefore fits R1's32 sends per entry. But publication is a relationship request (R1Request.type relate), and R1sections6.6/7.4 require its deciding entry to emit the correlated result too. With32 set links, published therefore produces at least33 sends; any declared attention adds further sends. I checked the actual handler row, G15 crosswalk and R1rev5 section7.5's unqualified 'Sends from one entry |32'. Reconcile the full sealed entry's count and byte/work budget, including its platform result and attention. Raise or separate the bound with an explicit R1/R4 decision, or choose a bounded durable fanout design that preserves all32 links and exact current publication/close correlation. Do not silently cut a valid last link, omit the result, shrink the demo's product scope or claim a declared loop's count covers the entire entry. One maximum fanout example is sufficient design evidence; no numerical test quota.\n\nKeep the note's own owed enumeration of all six issue handlers, G1–G15 and list/party/value/also bounds explicit, with executable definitions reviewed before source commission. R3def9c326 staging/hold/export/fence corrections and R162e51f0 complete assessment are live related inputs, not independent approvals. Fold actual job/dispatch/fanout witnesses into R4's compact useful-invariant plan without repeated whole-repo gates. The complete browser/durable/device, split/join/qualified review, public/cold-person/manual/replay/deployed and all-component removal outcomes stay intact. Internal changes requested under the original live R2 request/promise only; no runtime adoption, source filing override, sprint permission, compatibility requirement or fixed Jam gate.","body":{"head":"3b2a9cc9c2bf79d0f1ec2247c1b90316c6c154b8","scope":"R2 revision5 complete changed-byte assessment; design only","verdict":"internal-changes-requested"}}